That changes the plan in an important way. Lean becomes the source of truth and the compiler, not the runtime. It holds the specification and the proofs, and it generates code in whatever language each layer runs best in:
- CUDA or CuTe, Triton, HIP, Metal and Pallas for kernels;
- Rust or C for the scheduler;
- Python for anything that plugs into SGLang itself.

Two of my "won't shine" items then move to "shines". Hardware breadth becomes one specification with many lowerings. Kernels gain proofs of index, layout and tiling arithmetic, and of quantization-format conversions. The same data split supports this: of the 284 data-plane fixes, about 114 (40%) are in classes generation from a single spec addresses. That's platform-path 42, copy-drift 30, unit-mismatch 18, default-swallow 9, numerics-drift 8 and ownership 7. Revising the plan.

